# What the container build does NOT need out of this repository.
#
# The build context is this whole repository, because the kiosk gems are
# resolved through `path: "../kiosk-<gem>"` wherever a demo depends on them.
# That makes the context large, and everything below is either regenerated inside the image,
# machine-local, or has no bearing on a build.
#
# This file is an instruction to the build beside it: `Dockerfile` in this same
# directory. `bin/check-demo-copies` fails on a container ignore-file with no
# recipe at or above it, which is what three separate waves left behind here
# before the recipe existed.

# Version control and CI.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Machine-local toolchain pins and bundler state (the image installs its own).
.bundle
.gems
.mise.toml
mise.toml
.ruby-version
vendor/bundle

# Regenerated inside the container, or output of a run on somebody's laptop.
**/tmp
**/log
**/storage
**/coverage
**/node_modules
**/*.gem
**/.DS_Store

# The container recipes themselves: changing a compose file must not invalidate
# the image layers, because none of them is read at build time.
**/compose.yaml
.dockerignore
